/P 108 0 R
/E (The Vulnerability Assessment and Penetration Testing conducted on the north.sevenkingdoms.local Active Directory environment revealed multiple critical security weaknesses that collectively led to a full domain compromise.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
433 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 108 0 R
/E (The assessment demonstrated that an attacker, starting with no initial credentials, could successfully escalate privileges to NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM on the Domain Controller by chaining together common misconfigurations such as exposed credentials, weak password policies, insecure storage of sensitive data, and improper delegation settings.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
434 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 108 0 R
/E (This engagement highlights the importance of implementing strong security controls in Active Directory environments, particularly in areas related to credential management, authentication mechanisms, and access control. The absence of these controls significantly increases the risk of unauthorized access and complete infrastructure takeover.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
